<title>USA: North Sea crude priced out of U.S. market by LATAM.</title>
<headline>North Sea crude priced out of U.S. market by LATAM.</headline>
<byline>Jacqueline Wong</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. crude imports from the North Sea remained shut out this week even as prices fell and demand remained firm, which has been good news for Latin American crude exporters.</p>
<p>Traders said North Sea crude prices were cut to attract reluctant buyers, but end-users in the U.S. anticipated further declines and preferred to wait.</p>
<p>&quot;The differential between West Texas Intermediate (WTI) and Brent has been narrow for two months, which has been good for Latin American crudes,&quot; said one Gulf Coast trader.</p>
</text>
